{"id": "clm:5cf81d629b5fa3fa0b1493a05579ca85d23c41c653c98d78343f7190e46a28b4", "type": "statement", "text": "The inspected MongoDB unit tests include pre-epoch date-part extraction in UTC and America/New_York and DateAdd tests for positive and negative second and millisecond amounts. Those tests are useful fixture patterns, but do not by themselves prove cross-version 8.3 compatibility. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/datetime/date_time_support_test.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "structure", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:aba88a8da8c2cab3e344ef105dc657a81d5661f0cb26f8d2a0ec57bb16a932cf", "ev:ac95ab91c2054bc694b4bb03f82e1bad3646c91778275a73c3220c1e3ffbcaa9"]}
{"id": "clm:5ecc483e9c09ac1aed22595aa17fa12089533c11d7a33dbdf08d382a1b4bec08", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB documents that, starting in 8.3, $dateAdd and $dateSubtract return a result one second greater than previous versions when the input precedes 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z and unit is not millisecond. This describes a timestamp difference, not an execution-time increase. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/8.3.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.3/reference/operator/aggregation/dateadd/", "https://www.percona.com/blog/percona-server-for-mongodb-8-3-technical-preview-is-now-available/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/dateAdd/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/dateSubtract/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3db796a7b102f97488033a0d136ce414653aec4406888689d5853a831dbd886d", "ev:aa11b94e50c53ac2088672c2bb4e7e63e5af1880706b0ca2af65d358ea264281"]}
{"id": "clm:7065fde5bd479f20b6f24b0dd2beedacc083784bafae4040a45ab5d7b79209fb", "type": "statement", "text": "The release notes explicitly extend the compatibility warning to aggregations performing time-based calculations, including $setWindowFields and $densify. They do not say every output document or accumulator changes by exactly one second. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/8.3.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.percona.com/blog/percona-server-for-mongodb-8-3-technical-preview-is-now-available/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:43ad2f2707d4028202976ee35e53915d72117efeaefe4b168634f09a5fed032c"]}
{"id": "clm:c20b595af24112492fd02586bea94e64309fcf8744a097e944c12aa575a1e7fb", "type": "statement", "text": "Alibaba Cloud lists the same pre-epoch/non-millisecond condition but describes results as one second slower. MongoDB and Percona describe a timestamp that is one second greater; the Alibaba wording alone cannot substantiate a query-latency regression. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-09-10)", "source_url": "https://www.alibabacloud.com/help/en/mongodb/product-overview/features-of-mongodb-8-3", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "problems", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/8.3.md", "https://www.percona.com/blog/percona-server-for-mongodb-8-3-technical-preview-is-now-available/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:262cff031e384d27f7d8fc3d613973c80ce9599fc5cf30d687b10d8a15a481fa", "ev:43ad2f2707d4028202976ee35e53915d72117efeaefe4b168634f09a5fed032c", "ev:eddb896259cec174ba6ab3f4b61e3d6c7d1c1a7b48c28bdc71a83f33757fcaaa"]}
{"id": "clm:5ba9677c7d34b51dc585756c31b6ec20aca2f2453c74b1afa630a31aab585883", "type": "statement", "text": "The documented pre-epoch compatibility condition excludes millisecond units and inputs at or after the UTC epoch; it does not establish a general one-second shift for every date expression. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/release-notes/8.3.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.3/reference/operator/aggregation/dateadd/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/dateAdd/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/dateSubtract/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:3db796a7b102f97488033a0d136ce414653aec4406888689d5853a831dbd886d", "ev:aa11b94e50c53ac2088672c2bb4e7e63e5af1880706b0ca2af65d358ea264281"]}
{"id": "clm:9054842ff59fc98124b5aca57447874808cae5cd1f0f277a264e2d518a5cd168", "type": "statement", "text": "Do not assume replacing calendar units with fixed millisecond durations preserves semantics: $dateAdd uses the selected timezone for calculation, applies daylight-saving offsets, and adjusts month-or-larger additions at month ends. The implementation gives millisecond addition a separate direct-duration path. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/v8.3/reference/operator/aggregation/dateadd/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/datetime/date_time_support.cpp"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1d2a3c762c10a6f77ca025bba17436274409ab26e528e696154edea104b81c98", "ev:afdb59d109c74a79ac025424322d545114cb761aa2208d0c36a72447354e67de"]}
{"id": "clm:ca852932c2ec01af9b2df9a01bdf0c236b21b07b1a853b8b6719c0ccb7dd4ed6", "type": "statement", "text": "The inspected MongoDB master implementation floors negative fractional seconds in seconds(Date_t) and handles TimeUnit::millisecond by direct addition. These implementation details help select regression inputs; an unpinned master snapshot does not identify the commit responsible for the 8.3 compatibility change. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/datetime/date_time_support.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:416913bdf46e80b5532f1ea389558046da452645b7714d6e679c52fce715ba46", "ev:cc465c49fc99c56d5a3bcd935f9a108109b97428e876f775007317ab2af48ac9"]}
{"id": "clm:1d04f2e6228c2f79d7a8f44c1db2ef72c4ad1b37ba62bddd7e5c15e159377032", "type": "statement", "text": "Do not automatically replace day, month, or year arithmetic with fixed millisecond counts: both operators apply timezone rules, including DST where applicable, and adjust month-or-larger arithmetic to the last valid day of the month. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/dateAdd/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/reference/operator/aggregation/dateSubtract/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1cdb286ce660f2eb9f8887e7b0ba647c4456002eb2467e5f402b38f63822c650", "ev:6eab088727c3a3fb18a56dfd28606658cb884efafb36725e902cfb631d3526a1"]}
{"id": "clm:114928d21eccf0ff819f6049752c5255cb653b59aac3860b83b25054b54641c8", "type": "statement", "text": "In the reviewed master implementation, dateAdd returns date + Milliseconds(amount) immediately for the millisecond unit; other units pass through timezone/timelib processing. This supports separate millisecond controls but does not prove the implementation of a particular 8.3 patch. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/datetime/date_time_support.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:afdb59d109c74a79ac025424322d545114cb761aa2208d0c36a72447354e67de"]}
{"id": "clm:b779b73c450edfb4e0d50f8539e5d5d6df9218bcc1edcfd3a287729ede5fa210", "type": "statement", "text": "The reviewed upstream test file includes dateAdd tests for DST transitions, fixed-offset timezones, seconds, milliseconds, and overflow. These are useful test dimensions, but they do not constitute a before/after upgrade execution result. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-27)", "source_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mongodb/mongo/master/src/mongo/db/query/datetime/date_time_support_test.cpp", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Pre-epoch date arithmetic upgrade compatibility"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:473c8b19c15fdbba11ff85a2ca81420770cc4786cb053539321622eed8fdaef3", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:08fed06fb77271931567ecca16771e07b7fea983432f95767d9f6477b0758028", "ev:aba88a8da8c2cab3e344ef105dc657a81d5661f0cb26f8d2a0ec57bb16a932cf", "ev:e46643c0306d38747b1445e09fd049bd07e8136a36838661734489cbbb81c1d1"]}
